cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these results, please cite the paper. Until it has an identifier,
  cite this repository and the release tag you used. If you use Theorem C, please also
  cite the proof claim of Carlos Toledo, whose mathematics it formalises.
title: "Erdős Problem 1186 (k = 3): Lean formalization, verification scripts and computations"
version: "1.0.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dreadpiratechan/erdos-1186"
url: "https://quanalabs.com"
authors:
  - family-names: Snively
    given-names: Chandler
    affiliation: Quana Labs
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - monochromatic arithmetic progressions
  - Ramsey theory
  - semidefinite programming
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization, verification scripts and computations for the paper
  "Machine-checked results on the minimum number of monochromatic 3-term arithmetic
  progressions in two-colourings (Erdős Problem 1186, case k = 3)". For the constant delta_3
  of Formal Conjectures it proves 1675/32768 <= delta_3 <= 117/2192 (Parrilo, Robertson and
  Saracino), delta_3 >= 14324135/268435456, and delta_3 = 117/2192; the last is a Lean
  formalisation of an unrefereed proof claim by Carlos Toledo, whose mathematics it is.
  The results and the formalization were produced with AI systems; see docs/PROVENANCE.md.
